WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:06.550
Moments before the attack, the mayor of Gdansk
praising the fundraising effort for children

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.010
in need.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:19.110
As Pavel Adamowicz looked out at thousands
of people, a man lunged at him with a knife.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:24.240
The attacker then remained on stage, shouting
that he blamed the mayor's former party for

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:34.580
wrongfully imprisoning him, before he was
tackled to the ground.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.850
He was holding a knife in his right hand and
yelled that he'd spent five years in jail

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.700
because of the mayor's old party.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.440
He said his name, that he'd been in prison
and was tortured.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.620
We don't know how he managed to get on the
stage.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:57.160
Police have arrested the suspect, who they
said was a 27-year-old with a record of violent

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.550
crime.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:06.720
Our priority is finding out how the perpetrator
could get so close to the Mayor.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.040
We know he used a pass that said 'press' on
it.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.460
Adamovitch was rushed to hospital in a critical
condition, with wounds to the heart and abdomen,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.549
and underwent hours of surgery.

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:25.159
Poland has been left in shock by the attack
on this popular politician.

